// System include paths are not passed to cppcheck.
missingIncludeSystem

// Some suppressions only match in specific platform/configuration combos.
unmatchedSuppression

// Single translation unit analysis reports false positives for functions
// used across translation units.
unusedFunction

// Conflicts with project's coding style.
useStlAlgorithm

// GoogleTest macros inside namespaces: cppcheck's parser cannot follow
// TEST_F/TYPED_TEST expanded inside a named namespace and reports the closing
// brace as a syntax error. `core/cppcheck-suppressions.txt` and
// `common/.cppcheck-suppressions` suppress this id globally for the same
// reason. 102 of them here, which is every `error:` this product would
// otherwise report but one.
syntaxError

// Qt's moc vocabulary. `Q_SLOTS` in a dialog's private section is not known to
// cppcheck without Qt's own library configuration (`--library=qt`), which the
// build does not pass. `core` and `common` suppress the same id for ATL's
// BEGIN_SINK_MAP and Boost's macros.
unknownMacro

// Two shapes, neither of which cppcheck can see through, and there is no
// narrower id than `missingReturn` for either:
//
//   - Coroutines are not modelled, so `Awaitable<void> F() { (void)co_await
//     ...; }` reads as a non-void function that falls off the end. Same
//     rationale as `common/.cppcheck-suppressions`; ~250 such bodies here.
//   - `[[noreturn]]` on a function declared in a CONSUMED product is invisible,
//     because a standalone `client` checkout has no `core/` to include -- so
//     `base/check.h` does not resolve and `scada::base::NotReached()` looks
//     like an ordinary call. `controller/controller_fake.h:17` is the current
//     instance; expect more as `#include "base/..."` spreads.
//
// A genuine missing return in an ordinary function is hidden by this, which is
// the accepted cost until cppcheck models coroutines and the export layout
// gives the analysis job its sibling checkouts (ADR 0011 phase 9).
missingReturn
